te":"07/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"7 2026-06-26 Annual Governance Statement Report 25-26","url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s148188/7-2026-06-26-annual-governance-statement-report-25-26.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"26/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"7i 2026-06-26 Annual Governance Statement 2025-26 clean draft","url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s148189/7i-2026-06-26-annual-governance-statement-2025-26-clean-draf.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"26/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"10 2025-26 - External Audit Planning Report from EY Pension Fund - covering report - June 2026","url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s148210/10-2025-26-external-audit-planning-report-from-ey-pension-fu.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"26/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"11 HCC TM Outturn Report 202526","url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s148112/11-hcc-tm-outturn-report-202526.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"26/06/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-25","committee":"Hampshire Pension Fund Panel and Board","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"County Council","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Special County Council","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"HIWFRA Firefighters\u2019 Pension Board","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-19","committee":"Executive Lead Member for Universal Services Decision Day & Executive Member for Highways and Passenger Transport Decision Day","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Executive Lead Member for Children's Services Decision Day & Executive Member for Education Decision Day","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Executive Lead Member for Adult Social Care and Public Health Decision Day & Executive Member for Health and Wellbeing Decision Day","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"HIWFRA Audit and Governance Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Corporate Services and Resources Select Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Executive Member for Corporate Services Decision Day","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-11","committee":"Executive Lead Member for Adult Social Care and Public Health Decision Day & Executive Member for Health and Wellbeing Decision Day","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","time":"10.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Hampshire pension fund faces \u00a370m annual deficit relying on 5.9% investment returns","lead":"The Hampshire Pension Fund faces a \u00a370m annual shortfall between member contributions and pension benefits from 2026/27 to 2028/29. The fund plans to cover this deficit through \u00a3140m annual investment income whilst maintaining a \u00a360m operational cash buffer. This strategy depends entirely on achieving a 5.9% long-term investment return. The fund's Pension Panel and Board has adopted this approach based on an 80% confidence level, meaning a 1-in-5 chance that it will not fully fund all pensions.","iso":"2026-09-25","paper_title":"8a Investment Strategy Statement","paper_url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s151188/151188.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-25","committee":"Hampshire Pension Fund Panel and Board","paper_title":"PFPB Alternative Investments Portfolio Update report","paper_url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s151192/151192.pdf","headline":"Private Equity portfolio generated \u00a3168m cash distributions in 2025, net \u00a362m positive after capital contributions, showing strong cash generation.","detail":"The PE portfolio (\u00a3921m, 8.2% of fund) generated \u00a3168m distributions in 2025 representing 20% of opening NAV. After accounting for capital contributed that year, net cash was positive by \u00a362m. Portfolio has delivered 24 consecutive quarters of positive valuation growth. This consistent cash generation persists despite challenging market conditions and reduced M&A/IPO exit activity.","category":"income","matters":"Consistent positive cash from the largest alternative asset supports pension obligations and fund liquidity. Demonstrates the core portfolio is functioning well despite headline underperformance against some targets.","figures":"\u00a3168m distributions; \u00a362m net positive cash; 24 consecutive quarters positive valuation growth","quote":"during 2025 the portfolio generated \u00a3168m of cash distributions which represented 20% of the opening net asset value (NAV) of the portfolio for that year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-25","committee":"Hampshire Pension Fund Panel and Board","paper_title":"PFPB Alternative Investments Portfolio Update report","paper_url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s151192/151192.pdf","headline":"Private Equity and Infrastructure portfolios missing 3-year performance targets despite longer-term outperformance.","detail":"Private Equity returned 8.4% IRR versus 9-11% target (\u22120.6% miss); Infrastructure returned 6.0% versus 7.5-10% target (\u22121.5% miss). Both explained by J-curve effects from recent heavy capital deployment. However, longer timeframes show PE 5-year at 13.4% (4.4% above target) and Infrastructure 5-year at 8.2% (0.7% above target). Fund expects 3-year performance to improve as portfolio matures.","category":"other","matters":"Underperformance against recent targets across multiple asset classes suggests current capital deployment is creating performance drag. The extent to which this reflects normal J-curve dynamics versus sustained weakness matters to long-term fund sustainability.","figures":"PE: 8.4% vs 9-11% (3yr), 13.4% vs 9% (5yr); Infrastructure: 6.0% vs 7.5-10% (3yr), 8.2% vs 7.5% (5yr)","quote":"new commitments will always impact negatively on the shorter-term performance periods.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-25","committee":"Hampshire Pension Fund Panel and Board","paper_title":"PFPB Alternative Investments Portfolio Update report","paper_url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s151192/151192.pdf","headline":"Real Estate portfolio \u00a3243m below target with officers flagging that underweight will worsen as fund grows.","detail":"Real Estate holdings are \u00a31,077m against a combined target of \u00a31,320m (shortfall of \u00a3243m or 2.2% of fund). Underdeployment spans UK property (\u00a383m short), affordable housing (\u00a351m short), and timberland (\u00a3109m short). The document acknowledges 'risk that this underweight will continue to increase as the total value of the Pension Fund rises' and records that officers are discussing additional commitments with LGPS Central.","category":"capital","matters":"A material and explicitly acknowledged shortfall in a core strategic asset class indicates the fund is not achieving its intended asset mix. The warning that this gap will worsen is a structural governance issue with implications for meeting long-term return targets.","figures":"\u00a31,077m actual vs \u00a31,320m target; -\u00a3243m variance (-2.2% of \u00a311,226m fund)","quote":"the difference of 2.2% between the current NAV and the combined target and committed total, therefore there is a risk that this underweight will continue to increase as the total value of the Pension Fund rises.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-25","committee":"Hampshire Pension Fund Panel and Board","paper_title":"8a Investment Strategy Statement","paper_url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s151188/151188.pdf","headline":"The fund is actively working to divest from fossil fuel investments, narrowing its investment universe when returns of 5.9% are essential to managing the pension deficit.","detail":"The Pension Fund Panel and Board has committed to 'actively work towards disinvesting from fossil fuel investments' and is developing climate-aligned products with LGPSC targeting net-zero by 2050. The fund states disinvestment will not proceed if it causes 'significant financial detriment', but constraining the investable universe reduces portfolio flexibility.","category":"other","matters":"Fossil fuel disinvestment could reduce returns if energy equities outperform. The constraint narrows available assets when the fund is already dependent on strong returns to cover its \u00a370m annual deficit and meet its 5.9% target.","figures":"Net-zero emissions target by 2050 at the latest; approximately 11.5% of total fund allocation (one-third of private markets) targeted to impact investing","quote":"The Pension Fund Panel and Board (PFPB) have agreed to actively work towards disinvesting from fossil fuel investments.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-25","committee":"Hampshire Pension Fund Panel and Board","paper_title":"8a Investment Strategy Statement","paper_url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s151188/151188.pdf","headline":"Investment management transferred to LGPS Central pool from April 2026, concentrating operational risk with a single external provider managing funds for 14 councils.","detail":"Since 1 April 2026, LGPS Central (a Financial Conduct Authority-regulated investment pool) is responsible for implementing Hampshire's investment strategy and managing its portfolio. The pool includes 13 other councils. Hampshire retains its own investment strategy but LGPSC executes it through appointed investment managers and will execute rebalancing trades where needed.","category":"governance","matters":"Outsourcing to a third-party pool introduces counterparty risk: if LGPSC underperforms or fails, the fund's ability to achieve its 5.9% return target is compromised. However, pooling should lower costs and improve access to diversified investments.","figures":"14 councils in pool; LGPSC is responsible for quarterly reporting on investment manager and product performance against targets","quote":"From 1 April 2026 LGPSC are responsible for the implementation of this investment strategy and management of the Pension Fund's investments.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-09"},"name":"Hampshire CC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-23","since_iso":"2026-08-24","distress":false,"headline":"The Authority's outsourced finance services provider received a qualified ISAE 3402 assurance report due to control deficiencies during a system upgrade.","lead":"Control weaknesses at the outsourced service provider affect the reliability of transaction processing and financial data used in the Authority's reporting, creating residual risk in the financial control environment.","also":["31 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit Committee on 2026-09-24","n_findings":32,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Item 17 - EY Draft Audit Results - Appendix A","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.hants.gov.uk/documents/s150570/150570.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":146,"news_drafts_total":1}}